# EAS Build archives the ENTIRE git repo by default. This repo is a monorepo
# whose root is also a PHP/CodeIgniter website, with a Node backend under
# mobile-app/backend — none of which the React Native app build needs.
#
# So: ignore everything, then re-include ONLY mobile-app/frontend (the app).
# This drops the upload from ~411 MB to just the app source + assets.

# 1) Ignore every top-level entry (files, folders, and dotfiles like .git).
/*
/.*

# 2) Re-include the path down to the mobile app frontend.
!/mobile-app
/mobile-app/*
!/mobile-app/frontend

# 3) Inside the frontend, still drop things EAS rebuilds or doesn't need.
mobile-app/frontend/node_modules/
mobile-app/frontend/.expo/
mobile-app/frontend/dist/
mobile-app/frontend/web-build/
mobile-app/frontend/.env
